<main class="tutorial">
  <section class="intro">
    <div class="intro-text">
      <h1>How to set up a template</h1>
      <p>Choose a starting option on the dashboard, then build and test a reusable character sheet in the RPG Templates Studio.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="controls" aria-label="Tutorial controls">
      <span class="progress-label" id="progress-label">Step 1 of 10</span>
      <span class="progress-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="progress-fill" id="progress-fill"></span></span>
      <button type="button" class="btn" id="prev-step" disabled>Previous</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn" id="next-step">Next</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="track" id="steps-track" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Dashboard tutorial steps">
    <ol class="steps">

    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 1 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
          <img src="/images/dashboardss1.png" alt="Dashboard options to upload a template, open My Templates, or build from scratch">
        </div>
        <h2>Choose how to begin</h2>
        <p>On the dashboard, choose <strong>Upload a Template</strong> to import a .json file, <strong>My Templates</strong> to open templates you created or saved, or <strong>Build From Scratch</strong> to start a new design. From other pages, use <strong>Navigation</strong> to open <strong>My Templates</strong> or discover public sheets in <strong>Browse Templates</strong>.</p>
      </article>
    </li>

    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 2 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
          <img src="/images/uploadss2.png" alt="Template upload page with tutorial.json selected in the file picker">
        </div>
        <h2>Upload an existing template</h2>
        <p>Select <strong>Upload a Template</strong> when you have a compatible .json file. On the upload page, choose the file and select <strong>Upload</strong>. If the JSON has no title, its filename is used. The studio then opens the uploaded sheet so you can review and edit it.</p>
      </article>
    </li>

  
    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 3 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
          <img src="/images/templatess3.png" alt="My Templates page with the Edit button highlighted on a template you own">
        </div>
        <h2>Find a saved template</h2>
        <p>Open <strong>My Templates</strong> to see sheets you created or saved to your account. Choose <strong>View template</strong> to preview one, or <strong>Edit</strong> on a template you own to return to the studio. Choose <strong>Browse Templates</strong> in Navigation to explore public templates.</p>
      </article>
    </li>

    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 4 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">4</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
          <img src="/images/newTemplatess4.png" alt="RPG Templates Studio open to a new blank template canvas">
        </div>
        <h2>Start from a blank sheet</h2>
        <p>Select <strong>Build From Scratch</strong> on the dashboard or in Navigation when you do not have a file or saved template to reuse. The studio opens with an empty canvas, ready for you to add modules and arrange the sheet.</p>
      </article>
    </li>

    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 5 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">5</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
          <img src="/images/templatess5.png" alt="Developer and Playtest view buttons at the top of the template studio">
        </div>
        <h2>Switch between Developer and Playtest</h2>
        <p>Use <strong>Developer</strong> to edit the layout and settings. Use <strong>Playtest</strong> to interact with the sheet as a player, enter values, and test calculations or rolls.</p>
      </article>
    </li>

    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 6 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">6</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
          <img src="/images/templatess6.png" alt="Sheet settings section highlighted in the template studio sidebar">
        </div>
        <h2>Set up sheets and canvases</h2>
        <p>Open <strong>Sheet settings</strong> to name the canvas, set its grid square size, and change canvas, header, module, input, and accent colors. Select <strong>Add canvas</strong> for another tabbed area. Select a top-level module, choose a destination, and use <strong>Move module</strong> to move it. On a character sheet, each canvas scales the grid through its rightmost module to fill the available width.</p>
      </article>
    </li>

    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 7 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">7</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
          <img src="/images/newtemplatess7.png" alt="RPG Templates Studio module palette with controls for adding sheet modules">
        </div>
        <h2>Add modules from the palette</h2>
        <p>Click a palette button or drag it onto the canvas. <strong>Number</strong>, <strong>Text</strong>, <strong>Dice</strong>, <strong>Checkbox</strong>, and <strong>Notes</strong> handle common values. <strong>Math</strong> calculates values, <strong>Pages</strong> creates tabbed sections, <strong>Group</strong> organizes fields, and <strong>List</strong> creates repeatable rows.</p>
      </article>
    </li>

    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 8 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">8</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
          <img src="/images/templateStudioss8.png" alt="RPG Templates Studio with module settings open for editing field properties">
        </div>
        <h2>Configure and arrange modules</h2>
        <p>Open a module&rsquo;s menu and select <strong>Edit</strong> to configure its name, input, and other options in the <strong>Module settings</strong> panel. Drag modules to reposition them and use the corner resize handle to change their size. Select <strong>Remove</strong> in the module menu to delete one. Drag across an empty area of the canvas to select several modules. You can also copy, cut, and paste selections with Ctrl/Cmd+C, X, and V.</p>
      </article>
    </li>

    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 9 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">9</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
            <img src="/images/templatess9.png" alt="template module presets on the left">
        </div>
        <h2>Reuse a module preset</h2>
        <p>Load <strong>Ability check</strong>, <strong>Advantage attack</strong>, or <strong>Ability Score Bonus</strong> for connected, ready-made module setups. To create your own preset, select a group of modules, enter a preset name, and select <strong>Save selected modules</strong>.</p>
      </article>
    </li>

    <li class="step" aria-label="Step 10 of 10">
      <span class="step-token" aria-hidden="true">10</span>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="shot">
          <img src="/images/templatess10fr.png" alt="Playtest, Download .json, and Save controls highlighted in the template studio">
        </div>
        <h2>Test, download, or save</h2>
        <p><strong>Playtest</strong> verifies the finished experience. <strong>Download .json</strong> opens a naming dialog, updates the template name, and exports a copy to your computer. <strong>Save</strong> stores the template and asks for a title, description, and level: <strong>Private</strong> for only you, <strong>Public</strong> for public discovery, or <strong>Unlisted</strong> for access by link.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</main>

<script>
  (function () {
    var track = document.getElementById('steps-track');
    var cards = Array.prototype.slice.call(track.querySelectorAll('.step'));
    var prev = document.getElementById('prev-step');
    var next = document.getElementById('next-step');
    var label = document.getElementById('progress-label');
    var fill = document.getElementById('progress-fill');
    var total = cards.length;

    function padding() {
      return parseFloat(getComputedStyle(track.querySelector('.steps')).paddingLeft) || 0;
    }

    function currentIndex() {
      if (track.scrollLeft + track.clientWidth >= track.scrollWidth - 2) return total - 1;
      var edge = track.getBoundingClientRect().left + padding();
      var best = 0, bestDistance = Infinity;
      cards.forEach(function (card, i) {
        var d = Math.abs(card.getBoundingClientRect().left - edge);
        if (d < bestDistance) { bestDistance = d; best = i; }
      });
      return best;
    }

    function goTo(index) {
      var i = Math.max(0, Math.min(total - 1, index));
      track.scrollTo({
        left: cards[i].getBoundingClientRect().left - track.getBoundingClientRect().left + track.scrollLeft - padding()
      });
    }

    function update() {
      var i = currentIndex();
      label.textContent = 'Step ' + (i + 1) + ' of ' + total;
      fill.style.width = ((i + 1) / total) * 100 + '%';
      prev.disabled = i === 0;
      next.disabled = i === total - 1;
    }

    var ticking = false;
    track.addEventListener('scroll', function () {
      if (ticking) return;
      ticking = true;
      requestAnimationFrame(function () { update(); ticking = false; });
    });
    prev.addEventListener('click', function () { goTo(currentIndex() - 1); });
    next.addEventListener('click', function () { goTo(currentIndex() + 1); });
    window.addEventListener('resize', update);

    track.scrollLeft = 0;
    update();
  })();
</script>